MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_001: Aah! The risen dead are after us!
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_002: Run and don't look back. I'll take care of this!
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_003: Bless you!
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_004: They're everywhere... Damn it, there's no end\nto these things!
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_005: Hrah!
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_006: Haaah... Haaah... You saved me again,\nPromised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_007: Sorry. I was hoping to draw them out so the people\ncould escape, but I overextended myself.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_008: <NCA>"It was reckless to try that alone."
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_009: <NCB>"We could have lost you."
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_010: <ACA>I didn't go into it with a death wish. I thought if I\nkept struggling, I could fight my way out.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_011: <ACB>You'll never lose me without a fight. I have no\nintention of joining Balor's forces.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_012: That said, I know I can't last forever. When my\ntime comes, that will be that.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_013: If I ever become a Brimstone Lord, I want you to\nrun me through without hesitation.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_014: Send me back to the underworld as many times as it\ntakes. I know you're capable of it.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_015: Ngh...
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_016: I had a hand in this world's ruin. Whatever sacrifices\nI have to make are worth it to atone for that.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_017: Use me as a decoy, or a pawn, or whatever you have\nto in order to bring peace to this land.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_018: <NCA>"Don't be so eager to sacrifice yourself."
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_019: That's a noble sentiment, but it's not one you live by.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_020: You think only of others, day or night. You lead\nwithout rest, always fighting on the front lines.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_021: Is that not another way to sacrifice yourself? Taking\non our burdens without care for your own?
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_022: Mm...
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_023: But I won't press the point. It doesn't get\nus anywhere.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_024: Neither of us wants to see even one more person\ndie needlessly.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_025: And we both have karma weighing us down.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_026: I'm in no position to forgive you your sins. Not when\nI'm still working to expiate my own.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_027: What I can do is protect you until you're whole.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_028: <NCA>"I'll do the same for you."
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_029: Then the matter is settled.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_A_030: Come on, Promised One. There are still people who\nneed our help.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_001: Oh! Promised One!
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_002: I looked all over, but I thought you were gone from\nus. I can't believe you're back...
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_003: <NCA>"I'm sorry if I worried you."
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_004: That's putting it mildly. What you did, after urging\nme not to sacrifice myself...
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_005: But I'm no less glad to see you safe.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_006: Don't tell me you're planning to go help people right\nafter escaping certain death.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_007: <NCA>"You know me too well."
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_008: <NCB>"Wouldn't you do the same?"
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_009: <ACA>Of course I do. You and I are cut from the\nsame cloth.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_010: <ACB>I suppose I would. The two of us are alike in so\nmany ways.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_011: But the truth is...I feel like I'm slowly leaving behind\nmy old self.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_012: In our war with the underworld, I was driven mostly\nby my own guilt and desire to make amends.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_013: But now that we've beaten Balor and averted\ndisaster, I feel some small sense of satisfaction.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_014: Yet I still feel like I could do more. I want to help\nthe people...not for my sake, but for theirs.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_015: I'll never truly be rid of my guilt. But I do feel like\nI've been freed. Does that sound strange?
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_016: <NCA>"It's a blessing to be grateful for."
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_017: <NCB>"There might be hope for us yet."
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_018: If that's what you believe, then I can accept it.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_019: Let me go with you. I want to save as many as I can\nwhile my Heart Core still functions.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_020: <RSDS>Thank you. We should go at once. There are so many\npeople who need the deliverance we can bring.
MID_SE_Ism_Kou_S_021: Whether we have hundreds or thousands of years...\nWe'll walk this path until our bodies give out.